{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794374477788,"sessionID":"ses_e370068abffeXZLNWZFrPAqi4U","part":{"id":"prt_1c90da7b4001Rwqf8m4GPLlm5Z","messageID":"msg_1c90bd03c001tmg8NoQo7urbom","sessionID":"ses_e370068abffeXZLNWZFrPAqi4U","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794374477789,"sessionID":"ses_e370068abffeXZLNWZFrPAqi4U","part":{"id":"prt_1c90da7bc001y1F6oRwzuhCVf8","messageID":"msg_1c90bd03c001tmg8NoQo7urbom","sessionID":"ses_e370068abffeXZLNWZFrPAqi4U","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Build a Markdown notes app (Flask JSON API under `/api` + React/TypeScript/Vite frontend) per the spec, served by the existing `Dockerfile` on port 8000, SQLite data under `./data`, Tailwind CSS styling.\n\n## Important Details\n- Workspace `/workspace` (git repo, base commit `4915d99`); Python 3.13.5, pip 25.1.1, Node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1; **no docker** available for local verification.\n- Network works via proxies (PyPI index `http://172.30.98.3:3141/root/pypi/+simple/`, npm registry OK). `/tmp` dirs other than allowed patterns are blocked/denied — do temp/venv work inside `/workspace` (`.venv`, `.scratch`), clean up at end (also `.dockerignore` already excludes `.venv`, `__pycache__`, `*.db`).\n- pip constraint/hash behavior (verified): original `pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock` **fails** on pip 24.0 and 25.1.1 (\"Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode…\") because constraint hashes trigger require-hashes; **succeeds** on pip 26.3 (ignores constraint hashes). Decision: make `requirements.txt` a **complete pinned set of ALL 10 packages with `--hash` lines**, `requirements.lock` = same set with `# via` comments — works under all three pip behaviors.\n- pip `join_lines` semantics (from pip source): a line ending in `\\` continues to the next line; **comment lines terminate the continuation**. Therefore: in `requirements.lock`, last hash line before a comment MUST end with `\\`, comment lines must NOT end with `\\`; in comment-less `requirements.txt`, the **last hash line of each package must NOT end with `\\`** (otherwise the whole file becomes one invalid joined statement).\n- Existing lock hashes must be re-read from `git show HEAD:backend/requirements.lock` (the on-disk lock was overwritten by a broken first generation run). Known new hashes: `markdown==3.11.3` wheel `e1a31a112232504d753e5c01bb8c2de90d3f0ba986b063e10770cf7695b09e73`, sdist `81eb91631dc97ad1efbc76019ef0f80fe90ca49ddf81546752d79989c3bfff3e`; `nh3==0.3.7` wheel `70f5ac8626e899a4bab0ef74ca2f5bd602f49c7b739e6e5026b4afc6d63dac42`.\n- API design decisions: `POST /api/auth/register` → 201 `{\"id\",\"username\"}`; login → 200 `{\"token\",\"username\"}`; `GET /api/notes` items have **exactly** keys `id,title,published,updated_at`; full note has **exactly** `id,title,body,published,updated_at,author`; DELETE → 204; PATCH returns updated note 200; 401 JSON `{\"error\":\"authentication required\"}`; 404 JSON `{\"error\":\"note not found\"}`; duplicate username → 409; extra endpoint `GET /api/public/notes/{id}` (JSON, full note shape) added so the public page can show title/author; timestamps ISO-8601 UTC with ms (`...Z`); list ordering `ORDER BY updated_at DESC, id DESC`; markdown via Python-Markdown with `[\"fenced_code\",\"tables\"]` (no nl2br) then `nh3.clean()` sanitization (XSS).\n- Frontend design decisions: routes — `/` workspace, `/notes/{id}` public page (public link = `${origin}/notes/{id}`); auth token/username in localStorage keys `mdnotes_token` / `mdnotes_username`; no react-router (hand-rolled pathname state); \"New note\" POSTs an empty note immediately; editor autosaves debounced (~350ms PATCH) then fetches `/api/notes/{id}/html` for live preview (sequential promise chain + seq counter to avoid out-of-order saves); unmount flush of pending save; Tailwind v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin + `src/index.css` with `@import \"tailwindcss\";` (and `@plugin \"@tailwindcss/typography\"` for `prose` — verify at build); npm versions: tailwindcss 4.3.5, @tailwindcss/vite 4.3.5 (peer `vite ^5.2.0||^6||^7||^8`), @tailwindcss/typography, typescript `^5.9`, @types/react 19.3.0, @types/react-dom 19.3.0; no `tsconfig.json` yet (plan: standard Vite React TS config + `typecheck` script).\n- Test venvs already created: `/workspace/.venv` (pip 25.1.1), `/workspace/.scratch/v24` (pip 24.0), `/workspace/.scratch/v26` (pip 26.3).\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Explored scaffold: `backend/app.py` (health + SPA catch-all), `backend/requirements.txt` (flask, gunicorn), `backend/requirements.lock` (hashed, constraints), `frontend/` minimal Vite/React, `Dockerfile` (`pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock`, gunicorn `app:app`, port 8000), `.dockerignore`.\n- Wrote full new `/workspace/backend/app.py`: SQLite schema (users/tokens/notes + index), `get_db`/teardown with WAL+busy_timeout+foreign_keys, Bearer token auth (`auth_required`, `current_user`), register/login, notes CRUD with ownership rules, `GET /api/notes/<id>/html` + `GET /api/public/notes/<id>` + `/html`, `render_markdown` (markdown+nh3), `after_request` (`Cache-Control: no-store` for `/api/`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`), JSON 404/405 handlers, guarded SPA catch-all (`path.startswith(\"api/\")` → JSON 404; `is_relative_to` path-traversal check), `init_db()` called at import.\n- Edited the 404 handler to return `\"frontend build not found\", 404` when `frontend/dist/index.html` is missing.\n- Confirmed npm availability of all planned frontend packages; confirmed pip download of markdown/nh3 wheels and sdist.\n\n### Active\n- Regenerating `backend/requirements.txt` and `backend/requirements.lock` with the corrected join/continuation format; the latest generation script aborted on `AssertionError` because it re-parsed the already-modified on-disk lock (which now contains `markdown`/`nh3`), expecting only the original 8 packages. On-disk files are still in the **broken** first-run format (every line joined with `\\`).\n\n### Blocked\n- `backend/requirements.txt` / `requirements.lock` currently invalid (continuation-backslash bug); must be regenerated before any pip install test.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Regenerate both files from `git show HEAD:backend/requirements.lock` (original 8 packages) plus `markdown==3.11.3` and `nh3==0.3.7` with known hashes, using the corrected format: per-package block; `requirements.txt` last hash of each package has no trailing `\\`; `requirements.lock` last hash before each `# via` comment has trailing `\\`, comment lines have none (via-comments: flask/gunicorn/markdown/nh3 → `-r requirements.txt`; blinker/click/itsdangerous/jinja2/werkzeug → flask; markupsafe → jinja2 + werkzeug).\n2. Verify `pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock` succeeds in `.venv` (25.1.1), `.scratch/v24` (24.0), and `.scratch/v26` (26.3), then smoke-test the Flask app endpoints.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/workspace/backend/app.py`: full API implementation, just written (plus 404-handler edit).\n- `/workspace/backend/requirements.txt`, `/workspace/backend/requirements.lock`: broken on disk; must be regenerated (hashes source: `git show HEAD:backend/requirements.lock`).\n- `/workspace/Dockerfile`, `/workspace/README.md`: build/run contract (port 8000, `./data`, lock as constraints).\n- `/workspace/frontend/`: to be extended (package.json deps, vite.config.ts + tailwind plugin, `src/` components, `src/index.css`, tsconfig.json).\n- `/workspace/.venv`, `/workspace/.scratch/`: test venvs/artifacts to be removed during cleanup.","time":{"start":1794374477756,"end":1794374477759}}}
